b.summary('An 85-year-old man with prior 45 pack-year smoking exposure, CAD with three-vessel CABG, diabetes, hypertension and CKD presented with progressive abdominal pain, diarrhea and chest pressure. A renal ultrasound five years earlier showed moderate right RAS with PSV168 cm/s. Admission BP247/120 mmHg, HR126 and AKI/eosinophilia accompanied troponinT314→388 ng/L at six hours and EKG abnormalities. ACS and aortic dissection were considered then ruled out. Noncontrast CT showed marked aortic/proximal renal arterial calcification. The conflicting body/caption historical creatinine ranges remain unresolved.',sum([g[x] for x in ['history','baseline','old_us','presentation','initial_labs','repeat_trop','ekg','differential','exclusion','ct']],[]))
b.summary('Initial IV labetalol20mg and hydralazine20mg every4hours improved BP to129/54 and resolved chest pressure. Diarrhea improved, but serum creatinine rose to4.1 and BP rebounded188/81 despite home-antihypertensive uptitration. Echo showed generalized hypokinesis, LVEF37%, estimated RVSP51mmHg and an enlarged IVC with normal collapse. Doppler showed left renal atrophy and severe right RAS/PSV397cm/s. Acute decompensated heart failure/flash pulmonary edema required ICU transfer, BiPAP and clevidipine/furosemide infusion support.',sum([g[x] for x in ['initial_tx','initial_response','diarrhea_response','worsening','echo','current_us','hf','icu_support']],[]))
b.summary('Selective right angiography confirmed a critical calcified ostial lesion. IVheparin and wire crossing preceded sequential balloon dilation with persistent narrowing, then a5×15mm Herculink right stent expanded to5.5mm produced a patent lumen/brisk flow without distal embolization. Subsequent critical left ostial stenosis could not be crossed; no further left intervention was pursued because of advanced atrophy. Angio-Seal achieved hemostasis and no complications were reported. Postprocedural aspirin81mg/clopidogrel75mg dual therapy preceded clinical resolution over following days. Caption-only immediate creatinine3.9mg/dL downtrended to baseline by discharge; short-term outpatient creatinine was1.5mg/dL. No exact calendar date/long-term interval supplied. Suspected atheroembolism and proposed mechanisms remain qualified.',sum([g[x] for x in ['angio_access','angio_right','anticoag','wire','balloon','balloon_response','stent','stent_response','angio_left','left_attempt','left_decision','closure','post_antiplatelets','immediate_cr','resolution','discharge','followup','interpretation']],[]));b.finish()
